  "findings": [
    "ordinaryLift is the explicit five-row source table, with [A,B] handled before forming collapsed intervals; its definition assumes no recurrence. The reviewed theorem uses the canonical core nearFarInverse(coreNear,H0)(boundaryUnitArray) and cyclic predecessor/successor t-values as etaMinus/etaPlus, matching the source neighbor prescription.",
    "interval_five_cases is a proved exhaustive disjunction on every actual BoundaryInterval(n+1): avoidance; exact duplicate singleton; left=A with B<right; left<A with right=B; and strict spanning. The proof of ordinaryLift_equation funexts over every coordinate and consumes the disjunction in this exact order. It does not omit intervals touching A or B or impose an extra size condition.",
    "In the avoiding branch, not_duplicate_of_not_contains derives the needed collapse precondition from that branch. The imported coordinate theorem transports the complete composition sum and every actual gate/child, applies the actual core inverse equation, and identifies the collapsed unit entry. It includes unary compositions and requires no sign-square premise.",
